 F.10,"The obstruction at each successive central extension — Let $1\to A\to U\to V\to1$ be a central extension of topological $G_k$-groups, with $A$ abelian and with continuous local lifts for the cocycles under consideration. For a $V$-cocycle $c$, choose a continuous lift $\widetilde c$. Its defect \[ o_c(\sigma,\tau)= \widetilde c_\sigma\,\sigma(\widetilde c_\tau) \widetilde c_{\sigma\tau}^{-1}\in A \] defines a class in $H^2_{\rm cts}(G_k,A)$ independent of the lift. The class vanishes exactly when $c$ lifts. For a fixed representative $c$, its lifts modulo $A$-conjugacy form a torsor under $H^1_{\rm cts}(G_k,A)$. Passing to $U$-conjugacy further divides by the stabilizer of $c$ in $V$. Local conditions impose the corresponding local obstruction and localization conditions.",Proved,"sections/F.tex, F.10",,"Section 51, equations (371)-(373); folios 734 and 736; scans 173 and 178; explicit Selmer tasks in prompt Part F",No,"Full claim, assumptions and proof or recorded residual attack are in the indicated source."
